- **Pushing `dev` fires ZERO workflow runs — verify via the runs API, never by
  reading `on:` blocks.** Four `dev` pushes this session, each checked against a
  pinned pre-push run-id baseline: 0 every time.
- **The 2026-09-10 trunk directive's file table does NOT match this repo.** It
  names `.claude/bin/branch-landed-check.mjs` and
  `.claude/hooks/wip-closure-guard.js` — NEITHER EXISTS HERE. The live surfaces
  are `unlanded-work-surface.js` (resolves from `origin/HEAD`, not a constant) and
  `worktree-reap.mjs`.
- **A plan's site count is a hypothesis.** #2203 said the A2A well-known path was
  4 sites / 3 files; it was **16 sites / 6 files** — the original grep was scoped
  to `src/kailash/trust/a2a/` and could not see the integration test (9 sites) or
  the docs. Re-derive repo-wide before any rename.
- **A failing Tier-2 test may be a drifted MOCK, not broken production.**
  `mock_verify` omitted the real API's `action` parameter, so the correct
  production call raised `TypeError` → `-32603`. Check the REAL signature before
  changing production to satisfy a test.
- **`tools/sweep-redteam.py --all` returns `specs=0 … OK`** — it scans
  `workspaces/*/specs`, empty here. That sentinel is a vacuous green; run per-spec.
- **Cancelled duplicate CI runs surface as `fail` in `gh pr checks`.** Classify
  with `gh run list --commit <sha> --json conclusion` before believing a red board.
- **The local gate is ~29s, and fires only on Python/dep changes.** A report of it
  being slow points at TRIGGERING, not size.
- **zsh does not word-split unquoted variables**, so `$FILES` in a `cp`/`git
  checkout` is ONE filename and the command fails. A failing glob aborts the whole
  command, fabricating a `0`.

